  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA Canadian high pressure will linger over the area through\nTuesday before a weak cold front begins to push east across the\narea late Wednesday into Thursday. This frontal boundary is not\nexpected to result in any precipitation. Ahead of it on\nWednesday, temperatures will climb into the low to mid 70s\nbefore falling back into the upper 60s to low 70s on Friday. Low\ntemperatures will be quite cool, especially tonight into Tuesday\nmorning as amplified radiational cooling results in some areas\ndropping into the upper 30s especially in the typical cooler\nspots. Continue to opt for holding off on a Frost Advisory given\nthe expected scattered nature. Will continue to monitor\nconditions over the next couple hours.",
